---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: opx
description: A tiny CLI and a family of installable plugins for linting, building, and releasing front-end projects. Take as much opinion as you want.
---
<main id="main">
	<section class="hero">
		<h1>opx: the <em>optionally</em> opinionated front-end toolkit.</h1>
		<p class="lede">opx scans your repository, works out which languages and workflows you have, and runs the matching plugins from your own <code>node_modules</code>. Install only the opinions you want.</p>
		<div class="hero-actions">
			<a class="button" href="/getting-started/">Get started</a>
			<a class="button secondary" href="/cli/">CLI reference</a>
			<a class="button secondary" href="/api/">API reference</a>
		</div>
		<p class="facts">Free &amp; open source · MPL-2.0 · Node 24+ · Currently in beta</p>
{% highlight "sh" %}
yarn add --dev @allons-y/opx-cli
yarn opx init
yarn opx lint
{% endhighlight %}
	</section>

	<section class="features" aria-label="Highlights">
		<div class="feature">
			<h2>A tiny core</h2>
			<p>The CLI knows nothing about ESLint or changesets. It discovers plugins in your dependencies and delegates to them.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="feature">
			<h2>Opt in per tool</h2>
			<p>Enable only the detectors you want with <code>opx enable</code>. Nothing is installed or configured behind your back.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="feature">
			<h2>Composable configs</h2>
			<p>Every lint package exports a plain flat-config array. Spread it into your own <code>eslint.config.js</code> and layer your rules on top.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="feature">
			<h2>Release without ceremony</h2>
			<p>A lightweight changesets flow: record a change, version, and publish with one command family.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="landing-section">
		<h2>Packages</h2>
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><a href="/cli/"><code>@allons-y/opx-cli</code></a></td><td>The <code>opx</code> binary.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/api/"><code>@allons-y/opx</code></a></td><td>The engine: the <code>Detector</code> contract, config, state, and plugin loader.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/plugins/lint-js/"><code>@allons-y/opx-lint-js</code></a></td><td>JavaScript and TypeScript linting and formatting.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/plugins/lint-json/"><code>@allons-y/opx-lint-json</code></a></td><td>JSON, JSONC, and JSON5 linting.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/plugins/lint-md/"><code>@allons-y/opx-lint-md</code></a></td><td>Markdown linting.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><a href="/plugins/release/"><code>@allons-y/opx-release</code></a></td><td>A changesets-based release flow.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>
</main>
